const legacyPages = [
 ['how-to-remove-background','How to Remove an Image Background for Free','Learn to remove backgrounds, refine edges and export transparent PNGs with Clearcut.',[
 ['The short answer','Clearcut removes a photo background directly in your browser at no cost. Open the editor in desktop Chrome or Edge, select, drop or paste a JPG, PNG or WebP photo, and the AI model runs on your device. Compare the result with your original, correct the edges with the Erase and Restore brushes, then download a PNG without a watermark. No installation is needed, and background removal works without signing in.'],
 ['Step 1 — Choose your photo','Open the editor and select, drop or paste a JPG, PNG or WebP. The limit is 20 MB and 25 megapixels, and a sharp image with a clearly visible subject is easier to inspect and refine. If you want to try the workflow before using one of your own photos, load the sample photo in the editor first.'],
 ['Step 2 — Run the model on your device','Standard mode downloads about 98 MB on first use; Detailed mode can download up to 473 MB. Browser caching can help later runs, but files can be cleared or evicted. Keep the tab open and allow time for your device to finish. Your photo is processed in the browser.'],
 ['Step 3 — Refine and check the edges','Compare Original and Result to see where the mask went wrong. Use Erase and Restore with the circular brush cursor to correct it: Erase removes leftover background, and Restore brings back missing parts of the subject. A smaller brush gives you more control around hair, product edges and small gaps.'],
 ['Step 4 — Pick a background and download','Keep the checkerboard for transparency, choose a solid color, or add a background photo. Trim empty edges if the cutout leaves unused canvas around the subject, then download the PNG before closing the tab. The export keeps your photo’s dimensions and does not add a watermark. If you need an alpha-transparent file, the [transparent background guide](/transparent-background/) explains how PNG transparency behaves in other apps.'],
 ['What to expect and current limits','The editor handles one photo at a time, and batch processing and a public API are not available. HEIC photos from iPhones are not supported, and desktop Chrome or Edge is recommended. Both AI models compute the mask at 512 pixels internally, so very fine edge detail can still need brush work even though the export keeps the original dimensions. For subject-specific advice, see the [product photo](/remove-background-products/) and [portrait](/remove-background-portraits/) guides.']],
 [['Do I need to install software or create an account?','No. Clearcut runs in a desktop browser, and background removal works without signing in. A Google account is only used for optional features such as publishing a review or managing a Plus membership.'],
 ['Why is the first background removal slower?','The first run downloads an AI model to your browser: roughly 98 MB in Standard mode and up to roughly 473 MB in Detailed mode. Later runs can reuse the cached model files, although the browser can clear or evict that cache.'],
 ['Which files can I use with Clearcut?','JPG, PNG and WebP images up to 20 MB and 25 megapixels. HEIC photos from iPhones are not supported in the current release, and iOS browsers are not supported.'],
 ['Are my photos uploaded to a server?','No. The photo, the mask and your edits stay in browser memory on your device and are not uploaded to Clearcut’s payment backend. Model files are downloaded from Hugging Face and its content delivery network.'],
 ['Can I process several photos at once?','Not currently. The editor works on one photo per run, and batch processing is not available today.']]],
 ['remove-background-products','Remove Product Photo Backgrounds for Free','Create product cutouts and white-background listing images with Clearcut’s private browser editor.',[
 ['Cut out a product in your browser','Photograph one product, upload the JPG, PNG or WebP to Clearcut, and let the model run on your device. Check the cutout with Original and Result, clean the mask with Erase and Restore, then choose white or transparency and download a PNG at full output size without a watermark. Your product photos are never uploaded to a server.'],
 ['Prepare a clear product photo','Photograph one product in even lighting with space around its edges. A plain contrasting backdrop helps you inspect the cutout. Sharp focus matters more than the camera: a crisp outline gives the model cleaner edges to find, and it makes your brush corrections easier to judge.'],
 ['White background or transparent PNG','Choose white for a consistent catalog appearance, or transparency for packaging and design layouts. Check your marketplace’s own listing rules: Clearcut does not certify compliance. Export PNG to retain transparent areas. The [transparent background guide](/transparent-background/) explains how to verify alpha transparency in the exported file.'],
 ['Inspect the details','Check handles, cables, holes and reflective edges. Use Erase and Restore to clean the mask. Glass and shiny surfaces may retain background colors and need further editing. Zooming into the edges while comparing Original and Result is the fastest way to find leftover fragments or missing parts.'],
 ['Work through a catalog, one photo at a time','The editor handles one photo per run, so refresh the editor between products and download each PNG before starting the next. Batch processing is not available today, and there is no public API or marketplace integration. For the full tool-by-tool workflow, see the [background removal guide](/how-to-remove-background/).'],
 ['What Clearcut does not do','Clearcut does not generate realistic shadows or reflections, resize or compress images, or produce synthetic studio lighting. Keep the product’s real condition visible and follow your platform’s image rules. An honest listing photo serves you better than a polished but misleading one.']],
 [['Does Clearcut make my product photos compliant with marketplace requirements?','No. Clearcut removes and replaces backgrounds; it does not certify compliance with any marketplace’s listing rules. Always check the current requirements of the platform you sell on before uploading.'],
 ['Can I export a JPG for my product listings?','No. Clearcut exports PNG only, at full output size and without a watermark. PNG keeps transparency when you need it and avoids the extra compression artifacts of a re-encoded JPG.'],
 ['Can I process a whole product catalog at once?','Not currently. The editor works on one photo per run and batch processing is not available today. There is no public API for automation either.'],
 ['Why does my glass or shiny product keep some of the old background?','Transparent and reflective surfaces confuse edge detection because the product literally shows the background. Use the Erase and Restore brushes to correct the mask; heavy reflections may need retouching in another editor.'],
 ['Does Clearcut add product shadows for marketplace photos?','No. Clearcut does not generate synthetic shadows or reflections. A neutral white or solid background keeps the listing consistent; anything more needs to be photographed or edited deliberately.']]],
 ['remove-background-portraits','Remove Portrait Backgrounds for Free','Cut out people, change a profile photo background and refine portrait edges locally with Clearcut.',[
 ['The short answer for portraits','Open the editor in desktop Chrome or Edge, upload a sharp JPG, PNG or WebP portrait, and the model runs on your device. Refine the edge with Erase and Restore, then keep transparency, choose white or a custom color, and download a PNG at full output size without a watermark. Nothing is uploaded, which matters for photos of identifiable people.'],
 ['Start with a well-lit portrait','Choose a sharp photo with the person’s outline visible. Even lighting and a slight contrast between the person and the backdrop give the model cleaner edges to find. Use photos you own or have permission to edit, especially for pictures of other people.'],
 ['Refine hair, glasses and clothing','Hair, veils, glasses and clothing similar to the backdrop can need correction. Use a small Restore brush to recover the subject and Erase to remove remaining fragments. Work at a zoom level where you can see individual strands, and check the result against both light and dark backgrounds before saving.'],
 ['Choose the new background','Keep a transparent PNG for presentations, white for a clean profile look, or a custom color to match a brand. You can also place the cutout over a background photo. Whatever you choose, the export is PNG only at full output size. The [transparent background guide](/transparent-background/) covers alpha checks in other apps.'],
 ['Understand the result','Clearcut edits a subject mask; it does not retouch skin or reconstruct hair that was never visible in the photo. Both AI models use 512px internally. Full-size export preserves image dimensions but does not add native-resolution segmentation detail.'],
 ['Honest limits for official photos','Passport, visa and exam authorities typically specify exact dimensions, background shade and print requirements, and they generally expect an unedited, properly photographed original. Clearcut does not resize images or certify any photo as compliant. Check the official requirements of the authority you are applying to before using any edited photo. For the general tool workflow, see the [background removal guide](/how-to-remove-background/).']],
 [['Are my portrait photos uploaded anywhere?','No. The photo, the mask and your edits stay in browser memory on your device. This is especially relevant for portraits of identifiable people: nothing is sent to Clearcut’s payment backend.'],
 ['Can I use a Clearcut cutout as a passport or ID photo?','Usually not. Authorities typically require unedited photos meeting exact size, background and print specifications. Clearcut does not resize images or certify compliance. Follow the official requirements of the authority concerned.'],
 ['How do I fix hair that lost strands or gained background fragments?','Zoom in and use a small Restore brush to bring back missing strands and a small Erase brush to remove leftover background. Check the edge against both light and dark backgrounds, since a mask that looks fine on one can fail on the other.'],
 ['Why does my result look lower detail at the edges?','Both AI models compute the mask at 512 pixels internally. The export keeps your photo’s full dimensions, but it does not add native-resolution segmentation detail, so fine edges can still need brush work.'],
 ['Can I put my portrait on a custom background color or photo?','Yes. Keep the checkerboard for transparency, pick white or a custom color, or add a background photo in the editor. The export is PNG only, at full output size and without a watermark.']]],
 ['remove-background-animals','Remove Animal and Pet Photo Backgrounds','Make pet cutouts, inspect fur edges and save transparent animal PNGs with Clearcut.',[
 ['The short answer for pet photos','Upload a sharp photo of your pet, let the model find the animal on your device, refine fur edges with the brushes, and download a transparent PNG at full output size and without a watermark. Desktop Chrome or Edge is recommended, and your photo stays on your device.'],
 ['Choose a clear animal photo','Start with a sharp photo where ears, paws and tail are visible. Contrast between fur and backdrop makes the edge easier to inspect. A pet that fills the frame with a plain background behind it gives the model the cleanest outline to work with.'],
 ['Standard or Detailed mode','Standard mode uses the original 98 MB model and is enough for most pet photos; Detailed mode can download up to 473 MB and can help with fine fur against a similar-colored backdrop. If your computer has limited memory or a slow connection, try Standard first and only switch to Detailed when the fur edges clearly need it.'],
 ['Refine fur and small gaps','Inspect whiskers, the spaces between legs and the tail. Erase leftover background and Restore missing parts of the animal with small brush strokes. Fine fur on a similar-colored backdrop may need another editor; perfect edge separation is not guaranteed.'],
 ['Export for a creative project','Keep transparency for a collage or invitation, or add a color or background photo. Your selected image stays on your device. The current editor handles one photo at a time. The [background removal guide](/how-to-remove-background/) walks through every tool if you are new to the editor.']],
 [['Is Clearcut good with fur and whiskers?','Often, but not always. The model handles clear fur edges well, while fine fur against a similar-colored backdrop can need brush work. Whiskers and the gaps between legs are worth checking closely before you download.'],
 ['Which mode should I use for pet photos?','Start with Standard mode, the original 98 MB model, which is enough for most pets. Switch to Detailed mode, up to 473 MB, when fine fur against a similar-colored backdrop clearly needs more accuracy.'],
 ['Does the download have a watermark or reduced size?','No. The PNG downloads at full output size without a watermark. If you need to crop the empty canvas around the pet, use the Trim empty edges option before downloading.'],
 ['Can I make a cutout of my dog or cat for a print or invitation?','Yes. Keep the transparent background and place the PNG into your layout, or choose a solid color in the editor. The [transparent background guide](/transparent-background/) explains how to check the transparency in other apps.'],
 ['Does Clearcut blur or replace the background behind my pet automatically?','No. Clearcut removes the background and lets you choose the replacement yourself: transparency, a solid color, or a photo you add. It does not blur backgrounds or generate new ones.']]],
 ['remove-background-cars','Remove Car Photo Backgrounds for Free','Isolate a vehicle, refine the cutout and export a transparent or solid-background PNG for a listing or design.',[
 ['The short answer for vehicles','Upload a sharp photo of the vehicle, run background removal on your device, inspect the cutout, then download a transparent or solid-background PNG at full output size and without a watermark. Desktop Chrome or Edge is recommended, and the photo never leaves your device.'],
 ['Prepare the vehicle image','Use a sharp side or three-quarter view with the whole car in frame. Busy scenes and overlapping vehicles make it harder to judge the outline. A single car against a plain wall or open sky gives the model the cleanest edges to find.'],
 ['Inspect glass, mirrors and wheels','Check the gaps under the body, the mirror edges and the wheel spokes. Glass can retain reflections from the original surroundings because the window literally shows the background that was there. Brush tools correct the mask but cannot recreate what was hidden behind transparent windows.'],
 ['Make an honest listing image','A neutral background can make listing photos consistent. Keep the vehicle’s real condition visible and follow the platform’s image rules. Clearcut does not blur license plates, generate synthetic shadows, or offer dealership integrations; edit plates deliberately in a tool built for that if your listing requires it.'],
 ['Export and reuse the cutout','Keep transparency for a design layout, or choose white or a custom color for a consistent catalog. Trim empty edges if the cutout leaves unused canvas around the car. Download PNG before closing the tab, and run the editor again for the next photo: the editor handles one photo at a time and batch processing is not available today. The general workflow is in the [background removal guide](/how-to-remove-background/).']],
 [['Why do the windows keep reflections from the old background?','Glass is transparent, so the photo of the window contains the original surroundings. The mask marks the car as subject, but the reflections inside the glass remain in the pixels. Heavy reflections may need retouching in another editor.'],
 ['Can Clearcut blur or cover my license plate for a listing?','No. Clearcut does not blur license plates or hide details. Use an editor built for that if your platform or privacy needs require it.'],
 ['How do I clean up the wheel spokes and the gaps under the car?','Zoom in and use the Erase brush to remove leftover background fragments and the small Restore brush to bring back missing parts. Check the mirror edges too; thin protruding parts are the most common mask errors on vehicles.'],
 ['Can I get a white studio-style background for my car photos?','You can select white or a custom solid color in the editor for a consistent catalog look. Clearcut does not add synthetic shadows or studio lighting, so the result is a flat, honest background rather than a simulated studio shot.'],
 ['Can I process a whole set of listing photos at once?','Not currently. The editor handles one photo per run and batch processing is not available today. There is no public API or dealership integration for automation.']]],
 ['transparent-background','Make a Transparent Background PNG for Free','Remove a photo background and keep alpha transparency when exporting a PNG with Clearcut.',[
 ['The short answer: a real transparent PNG','Upload a JPG, PNG or WebP up to 20 MB and 25 megapixels, run background removal on your device, and leave the checkerboard selected. Download the PNG to keep real alpha transparency at full output size and without a watermark. The complete workflow, including edge refinement, is in the [background removal guide](/how-to-remove-background/).'],
 ['How PNG transparency works','PNG stores an opacity value for each pixel, so a pixel can be fully transparent, fully opaque, or partly transparent at the edge of your cutout. The editor’s checkerboard is a visual guide and is not included in the downloaded image. Partly transparent edge pixels can help the cutout blend into a layout.'],
 ['Verify the transparency before you download','Compare Original and Result to check the cutout, and use Erase and Restore to correct the mask where it went wrong. Some image viewers display transparent areas against white or black, which can look like a solid background. Place the exported file over a colored page or background to confirm the transparency is really there.'],
 ['What Trim empty edges does','Trim empty edges crops the unused transparent canvas around the subject, so the download contains just the cutout. Leave it off to keep the photo’s original dimensions when your layout expects them. Trimming changes the canvas size only, not the level of transparency in the pixels themselves.'],
 ['Why PNG and not JPG','The JPEG format cannot store per-pixel transparency, so a transparent cutout has to be a PNG. Clearcut exports PNG only, at full output size and without a watermark. If you need a solid background instead, choose white, a color, or a background photo in the editor.'],
 ['Graphics and logos','You can try graphics with a clear foreground, but fine lettering and internal spaces may need correction with the brushes. The AI identifies subjects rather than selecting every logo color precisely. Clearcut does not vectorize artwork or export SVG. For cutouts you plan to place on white in a catalog, see the [product photo guide](/remove-background-products/).']],
 [['Is the checkerboard included in my downloaded PNG?','No. The checkerboard is only a visual indicator of transparency in the editor. The downloaded PNG contains alpha transparency wherever the background was removed.'],
 ['Can I save a transparent JPG?','No. The JPEG format cannot store per-pixel transparency, so a transparent cutout has to be exported as a PNG. Clearcut’s download button exports a PNG at full output size.'],
 ['What does the Trim empty edges option do?','It crops the empty transparent canvas around the subject so the PNG contains just the cutout. Leave it unchecked if you need the original image dimensions, for example for a layout that expects them.'],
 ['My PNG looks like it has a white or black background in another app. Is the transparency gone?','Probably not. Many viewers render transparent pixels against white or black by default. Place the file over a colored background or a web page to confirm the alpha channel is present.'],
 ['Do partly transparent edge pixels survive the export?','Yes. Edge pixels can be partly transparent, which helps the cutout blend into a new background. Over-erasing hardens the edge, so use the Restore brush to bring back soft areas you removed by mistake.']]],
 ['about','About Clearcut Remove BG','Learn what Clearcut supports, how local image processing works, and what the free editor and Plus membership provide.',[
 ['An independent image editor','Clearcut removes backgrounds in your browser with an open-source BG0/BiRefNet-based engine. The website is hosted through GitHub Pages and Cloudflare. Clearcut is independent and is not affiliated with remove.bg or Canva.'],
 ['What works today','The editor supports JPG, PNG and WebP up to 20 MB and 25 megapixels, original/result comparison, Erase and Restore, background replacement, trimming and PNG export without a watermark. Desktop Chrome or Edge is recommended. iOS and HEIC are unsupported.'],
 ['Clear pricing and limitations','Processing currently works without sign-in. Plus is a one-time ₹90 payment for 30 days, renewed manually. The backend stores the account badge and expiry. Daily limits are guidance and are not enforced today; Plus does not yet unlock batch processing. Read the current pricing before paying. Demonstration artwork is original AI-generated artwork, not measured model output.'],
 ['Editorial standards','Clearcut maintains its guides against the current editor and the sources cited on each page. Product claims are updated when behaviour changes, and dated India guidance is reviewed at least every 90 days or sooner when an official source changes. Illustrations and AI-generated artwork are labelled; measured benchmarks must publish their device, browser, model, input and date. Send factual corrections through the Contact page.']]],
 ['privacy','Clearcut Privacy Policy','How Clearcut handles local images, Google sign-in, reviews, payment references, model downloads and membership data.',[
 ['Photos and edits','Selected photos, masks and edits remain in browser memory; they are not uploaded to the payment backend. Clearing the editor or closing the tab discards the editing session. PNG downloads are stored where your browser saves files. Model files may remain in browser cache. Closing a tab is not a guarantee of forensic memory erasure.'],
 ['Accounts and payments','Firebase provides Google sign-in and can remember the login until you sign out or clear browser data. Cloudflare D1 stores the validated account ID, verified Google email, order and payment references, plan, expiry and webhook identifiers. These records restore membership and prevent duplicate payment processing. Razorpay hosts payment entry; Clearcut does not store card numbers, CVVs, banking passwords or UPI credentials.'],
 ['Third-party connections and performance analytics','GitHub Pages and Cloudflare serve the website, Google/Firebase provide authentication, and Razorpay handles payments. Model requests go to Hugging Face and its CDNs; the runtime downloads from jsDelivr. Those providers receive ordinary network metadata, such as IP addresses and request headers. Cloudflare Web Analytics currently injects a cookie-free performance beacon. It sends the page URL, referrer and browser performance measurements such as loading, paint and layout-shift timings to Cloudflare; it does not receive your selected photo, mask or edits. Cloudflare states that the beacon does not use cookies or browser storage and that source IP addresses received during request handling are discarded at the nearest data centre rather than stored in its core analytics databases or logs.'],
 ['Retention and requests','Account and payment metadata currently remain in the backend; an automatic deletion schedule and self-service deletion are not implemented. Payment records may need retention for support and applicable obligations. See Contact for the current support channel. Never post private account or payment information in a public issue. This policy describes the implementation reviewed on 14 November 2026 and will be updated when practices change.'],
 ['Public reviews','Signed-in users may submit one display name, rating and written review. Reviews are stored with the Firebase account ID and published immediately. Public responses do not expose account IDs or email addresses. Administrators may remove abusive or irrelevant content; deleting a review removes the saved review. Moderation decisions are logged for accountability.'],
 ['Contact for privacy requests','Email yxsingh2@gmail.com to request correction or deletion of your account information. Identify the Google account concerned; Clearcut may need to verify account ownership. Do not send passwords or payment instrument credentials. Financial records that must be retained may be excluded from deletion.']]],
 ['contact','Contact Clearcut and Get Help','Troubleshoot the editor, report a technical issue and learn what to do if a payment is charged but membership is not active.',[
 ['Processing help','Use current desktop Chrome or Edge, check your connection for the first model download, and try Standard mode if memory is limited. Save your edits before refreshing. iOS and HEIC are unsupported. See the background removal guide for the complete workflow.'],
 ['Charged but Plus is missing','Do not pay again. Sign into the same Google account used at checkout and return to the site so membership can refresh. Keep the Razorpay payment receipt for private support. A different Google account does not inherit the original account’s membership.'],
 ['Private support and data requests','Email yxsingh2@gmail.com for membership, payment activation, account correction or deletion requests. For a payment problem, include the Google account used at checkout, the payment date and Razorpay reference. Never send card numbers, CVVs, passwords, OTPs or UPI PINs. For technical bugs, describe your browser, operating system, error and steps to reproduce. The GitHub issue tracker is public: keep personal data out of reports.'],
 ['Renewal and paid-launch status','Access lasts 30 days and renewal requires another deliberate payment; there is no automatic subscription charge. Refund terms still need to be finalized before a broader paid launch. Contact support before paying again if a transaction is unclear.']]]
].map(([slug,title,description,sections,faqs,fields]) => {
 const o=typeof fields==='object'&&fields!==null?fields:{};
 return {slug,title,description,sections,faqs:faqs||[],metaTitle:o.metaTitle||title,h1:o.h1||title,lang:o.lang||'en',images:o.images||[],tables:o.tables||[],explicitLang:!!o.lang,lastModified:o.lastModified||policyDates[slug]||releaseDate,isGuide:!policySlugs.has(slug)};
});
const links = () => pages.map(p => `<li><a href="${site}${p.slug}/">${escape(p.title)}</a></li>`).join('');
// Editorial sanitizers: strip internal implementation details (alpha thresholds, forensic RAM erasure)
// from published india-page prose; practical limits (512px masks, single-step undo, model sizes) stay.
const sanitizeProse = value => value
 .replace(/\s*\(alpha\s*>\s*\d+\)/g,'')
 .replace(/\s*\(halaanki tab band karna forensic RAM erasure ki guarantee nahi hota\)/g,'')
 .replace(/\s*\(closing a tab is not a forensic RAM-erasure guarantee\)/g,'');
const mdProse = value => {
 const sanitized=sanitizeProse(value);
 if(!sanitized.trim())throw new Error('Prose sanitizer produced empty text');
 return md(sanitized);
};
